 14: 419\n    15: 419 16: 419\nGraphics:\n  Device-1: Advanced Micro Devices [AMD/ATI] Navi 33 [Radeon RX 7600/7600\n    XT/7600M XT/7600S/7700S / PRO W7600] driver: amdgpu v: kernel\n  Device-2: Advanced Micro Devices [AMD/ATI] HawkPoint1 driver: amdgpu\n    v: kernel\n  Device-3: Microdia Integrated Camera driver: uvcvideo type: USB\n  Display: wayland server: X.org v: 1.21.1.18 with: Xwayland v: 24.1.8\n    compositor: kwin_wayland driver: X: loaded: amdgpu\n    unloaded: modesetting,radeon dri: radeonsi gpu: amdgpu\n    resolution: 1920x1080~165Hz\n  API: EGL v: 1.5 drivers: kms_swrast,radeonsi,swrast\n    platforms: gbm,wayland,x11,surfaceless,device\n  API: OpenGL v: 4.6 compat-v: 4.5 vendor: amd mesa v: 25.1.9 renderer: AMD\n    Radeon 780M Graphics (radeonsi phoenix LLVM 20.1.8 DRM 3.64\n    6.17.5-200.fc42.x86_64)\n  API: Vulkan v: 1.4.313 drivers: radv surfaces: N/A\n  Info: Tools: api: clinfo, eglinfo, glxinfo, vulkaninfo\n    de: kscreen-console,kscreen-doctor gpu: radeontop wl: wayland-info,wlr-randr\n    x11: xdriinfo, xdpyinfo, xprop, xrandr\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534681677/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534896374","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112788#issuecomment-3534896374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112788","id":3534896374,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ssjz2","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T22:24:07Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T22:24:07Z","body":"Yes, this was only tested with an Nvidia GPU and the proprietary driver. I had no alternative gpu back then\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534896374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3535424682","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112788#issuecomment-3535424682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112788","id":3535424682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sukyq","user":{"login":"Sch1nken","id":11414422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDE0NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11414422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken","html_url":"https://github.com/Sch1nken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T02:24:40Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T02:25:09Z","body":"Since the original implementation mentions using lspci because it is widespread on most distros, I fiddled around a bit with it (not super familiar with its parameters).\nUsing `lspci -k` gives me a list of devices and their kernel drivers. Using `lspci -k -s <bus:device.func>` only outputs the specified device like so:\n```\nlspci -k -s 04:00.0\n04:00.0 VGA compatible controller: Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. [AMD/ATI] Renoir [Radeon Vega Series / Radeon Vega Mobile Series] (rev c6)\n        Subsystem: AIstone Global Limited Device 109f\n        Kernel driver in use: amdgpu\n        Kernel modules: amdgpu\n```\n\nI am not sure if the kernel driver in use can differ from some sort userland driver (though probably unlikely for GPUs?) and also not sure if this would work for non-amd systems.\n\nTL:DR:; `lspci` can output the used driver afaict","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3535424682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536250101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112788#issuecomment-3536250101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112788","id":3536250101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SxuT1","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T09:29:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T10:25:33Z","body":"_EDIT_: made a mistake, revised the comment\n\noutput on my laptop:\n\n```sh\n# replicating what Godot would do in `OS_LinuxBSD::lspci_get_device_value`:\n$ lspci -d 8086:7d55 -k\n00:02.0 VGA compatible controller: Intel Corporation Meteor Lake-P [Intel Arc Graphics] (rev 08)\n\tDeviceName: Onboard IGD\n\tSubsystem: Hewlett-Packard Company Meteor Lake-P [Intel Arc Graphics]\n\tKernel driver in use: i915\n\tKernel modules: i915, xe\n```\n\ngodot adds the device class (`0300`, `0302`, or `0380`) to `lspci -d 1002:7550 -vmm` (see below). Though, at least on my laptop adding the device class made no difference\n\n\n---\n\nto find any issue, the following process should be done:\n```sh\n# use godot and add to your feedback the output of:\nRenderingServer.get_video_adapter_name()\nRenderingServer.get_video_adapter_vendor()\n\n# now use the command line tool:\n$ lspci -n\n# find _all_ lines that contains `0300`, `0302`, or `0380` and add it to your feedback\n# example: `02:00.0 0300: 10de:13c2 (rev a1)`\n# try all the valid lines from the previous output with the following steps (until you get your driver name):\n# take the value after `0300` (or whatever you have at that spot): here `10de:13c2` and then like so:\n$ lspci -d 10de:13c2:0300 -vmm # but with your values\n# add the output to your feedback\n# check the output and look for the line starting with \"Device\". it should contain sth. similar\n# to the output of RenderingServer.get_video_adapter_name().\n$ lspci -d 10de:13c2 -k\n# add the output to your feedback\n# there should be a line with `Kernel driver in use` that contains your driver name\n```\n\n\n---\n\n`inxi` sounds useful, but sadly has been archived almost 2 years ago","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536250101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536986020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112788#issuecomment-3536986020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112788","id":3536986020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S0h-k","user":{"login":"Sch1nken","id":11414422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDE0NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11414422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken","html_url":"https://github.com/Sch1nken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T22:28:48Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T22:28:48Z","body":"Here is what happens on my machine (AMD Laptop with iGPU):\n\n```gdscript\nRenderingServer.get_video_adapter_name() # = AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR)\nRenderingServer.get_video_adapter_vendor() # = AMD\n```\n\n```\n$ lspci -n\n...\n04:00.0 0300: 1002:1636 (rev c6)\n...\n```\n\n```\n$ lspci -d 1002:1636:0300 -vmm\nSlot:   04:00.0\nClass:  VGA compatible controller\nVendor: Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. [AMD/ATI]\nDevice: Renoir [Radeon Vega Series / Radeon Vega Mobile Series]\nSVendor:        AIstone Global Limited\nSDevice:        Device 109f\nRev:    c6\nProgIf: 00\nIOMMUGroup:     5\n```\n\n```\n$ lspci -d 1002:1636 -k\n04:00.0 VGA compatible controller: Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. [AMD/ATI] Renoir [Radeon Vega Series / Radeon Vega Mobile Series] (rev c6)\n        Subsystem: AIstone Global Limited Device 109f\n        Kernel driver in use: amdgpu\n        Kernel modules: amdgpu\n```\n\nI had a peek at how neofetch gathers GPU data but it's too late for me today to dive further. Its some bash script in conjunction with lspci | awk.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536986020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3538471069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112788#issuecomment-3538471069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112788","id":3538471069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S6Mid","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/user